{
  "text": "Seo for those of you that don't know means search engine optimization which basically means Trying to get higher up in the search results for Google see Google isn't great at figuring out what's on a webpage well actually they're Pretty good at it now and they're getting better but still they reward people that make their job easier and There's two main aspects of Seo When google's Trying to figure out How high it should rank a certain website for a certain search term it not only figures out what that page is about but How many Links Come Into it the first one's called onpage seo And you can help Google figure out what your website's about the second one is called offpage Seo or link Building but We're not going to talk about that in this video because That's a little bit more Advanced but onpage Seo is critical when you're first starting out your store When Google Comes to your site it might not know what it's about but What it'll do is it'll search the text it'll search the images it'll search a bunch of different factors and try to figure out What's going on in the site in this video There's five main areas We Going to talk about on how you can improve your onpage Seo so Google rank your site higher the first one is using keywords second one is using heading tags third one is using Meta title and Meta description tags fourth one is using all image tags and generally making your images easier for Google to read and lastly the structure Of Your website Which is critically important the first one is using the proper keywords We talked about this in the previous segment but at the end of the day you need to name your products with the correct keywords pepper it in throughout the product description and throughout your website make sure that you're targeting those Words the next thing is using the header tags and header tags the H1 tags H2 tags H3 tags and etc but basically What it is is the heading that Lets Google know this page is about x subject you might want to use An H1 tag That is the name of the product because then Google knows that that page is about this product and these keywords in the H1 tag are extremely important you can also use H2 tags It's kind of like sub areas so If I wanted to write a blog post about the best Nut butters in the world I could have the H1 tag be best Nut butters in the world and then H2 tag could be almond Butter h another H2 tag could be peanut butter another H2 tag could be walnut Butter etc etc that way Google knows this page is about best Nut butters and then these different sections are about the different types of Nut butters the Meta title and Meta description sound really Fancy and complicated but That's What shows up When people are searching for your website on google So this is extremely important because Google not only determines How relevant all your information IS they also use How often people click on that so the Meta title and Meta description are almost like An advertisement for your website And you want to make sure that It's not only Keyword rich but that It's user friendly and that humans are actually going to want to click on that title to get to your website the next subject We Going to talk about is the images and google's really bad at reading images It can read text Pretty well But when it sees An image It has no idea What's Going On So you need to help it out you can do this by using the alt image tags which describes What's going on in the picture so for instance If i was going to put this picture up i'd want to say It's Highway stand shorts that way Google knows Oh not only is this page about Highway stand shorts but this product specifically is about Highway stand shorts On Top Of that you can do other things such as naming the image the Keyword that you want to rank for for instance I'd name this Highway Dan shorts jpeg And you can also add in titles of the image and other things like that so that Google knows that that image is of whatever certain Keyword you want to rank for the last thing We're going to talk about is structuring your website properly and different platforms different shopping carts have different ways of doing this But when you're structuring your website you want to make sure your urls actually contain your keywords but not just that Going Back To My example I have a category called dance shs and then within that I have the different dance shorts I have regular dance shorts booty shorts Highway shorts and the way that the URL is structured is so that Google Can easily Read it and say that Ok all these different product pages are all part of this bigger category of Dance shorts but dance shorts also is a Keyword I'm trying to rank for On Top Of that when you're structuring your website you want to have Links throughout your website pointing to your most important pages or At least the pages that you're Trying to rank for the most I recently Found out that a lot of my traffic was going to the certain page I was very surprised when I saw this but I realized The Reason for it on my main homepage There is a Giant banner that had a link to this page you see If you're Trying to get to rank something higher up it might help to add it to your homepage or add it to different pages throughout your website such as blog posts and stuff like that because if your website has 100 Links going to one page Google knows that of all the pages on your website this page is very important so put more weight into this page i created an Seo checklist that you can get for free by clicking up here this checklist includes everything you need to know to get the page One On Google It has things like onpage Seo offpage seo link Building strategies Really I put all the secrets and tactics that I know into this list and It's a nice easy format So You can go off one by One Check it to make sure that your site's ready to go and it's properly Seo so click up there to get it now if you enjoyed this e-commerce News episode make sure you Subscribe Down below I'm going to give you new episodes every week making sure you stay ahead on the latest and Greatest in e-commerce News and the Trends you don't want to get cau behind and if you haven't already make sure you sign up for my e-commerce success pack There's a ton of great stuff in there basically when you sign up on going to send you checklists marketing ideas other stuff like that and it's going to be just tons of value in there I promise but Thank you guys for watching this and remember We have new e-commerce news episodes every Monday tips and tricks on tuesdays and q&a on wednesdays so if you have any questions Please leave it in the comments below",
